WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:06.207
Swallow flew around the statue.

2
00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:10.749
"Where is the water coming from?" he thought.

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:17.137
Then he saw the statue's eyes. He gasped.

4
00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:23.374
"Are those tears streaming from his eyes? It can't be."

5
00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:26.467
But it was!

6
00:00:26.468 --> 00:00:30.500
Swallow perched on the statue's shoulder for a closer look.

7
00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:36.666
And indeed, tears were flowing from the statue's eyes.

8
00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:44.791
"But statues don't cry," Swallow said. "Especially not happy statues."

9
00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:50.504
"Well, looks aren't everything!" a voice said.

10
00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:55.249
"Who said that?" Swallow looked around.

11
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.832
There was no one there.

12
00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:03.574
Swallow shook his head. "I've got to get out of this town.

13
00:01:03.575 --> 00:01:06.791
Strange things are happening!

14
00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:10.379
Statues that cry. A voice from nowhere.

15
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.374
I will leave for Egypt at first light!"

16
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:18.853
"At least you can leave," the voice said.

17
00:01:18.854 --> 00:01:24.970
Swallow couldn't believe it. The statue was talking to him!

18
00:01:24.971 --> 00:01:30.828
He flapped his wings. "Are you alive in there?"

19
00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:40.932
"Yes, I am." The statue sighed deeply.

20
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:46.057
"How did you get inside a statue?" Swallow asked.

21
00:01:46.058 --> 00:01:50.222
"It was a magic spell.

22
00:01:50.223 --> 00:01:54.962
I used to be a boy, and I was so happy.

23
00:01:54.963 --> 00:02:00.070
I didn't have a care in the world," the statue said.

24
00:02:00.071 --> 00:02:04.850
"My parents, the king and queen, loved me very much.

25
00:02:04.851 --> 00:02:14.868
They said I was perfect. Everyone at the castle called me the Happy Prince."

26
00:02:14.869 --> 00:02:21.618
"You still look happy. So why are you crying?" Swallow asked.

27
00:02:21.619 --> 00:02:27.077
"Because now I'm sad all the time," the statue said.

28
00:02:27.078 --> 00:02:30.725
"I guess I'd be sad too, if I was a statue.

29
00:02:30.726 --> 00:02:38.116
Then I couldn't fly fast like this!" Swallow zoomed around the statue.

30
00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:47.407
"Or look at beautiful things—like you and my darling. Well, never mind."

31
00:02:47.408 --> 00:02:51.681
"I wish I was a boy again," the statue said.

32
00:02:51.682 --> 00:02:59.366
"But that's not why I'm crying. It's because so many people are sad."

33
00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:05.282
"They are?" Swallow said. "I never noticed."

34
00:03:05.283 --> 00:03:10.894
"My nursemaid tried to teach me to think about others.

35
00:03:10.895 --> 00:03:15.491
But I never listened," the statue said.

36
00:03:15.492 --> 00:03:19.816
"And now all I see is the misery of the world.

37
00:03:19.817 --> 00:03:25.629
Yet I am helpless to do anything about it."

38
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:29.558
"Your smile must make people happy," Swallow said.

39
00:03:29.559 --> 00:03:38.045
The statue scoffed. "My smile doesn't feed them.

40
00:03:38.046 --> 00:03:42.803
It doesn't keep them warm at night."

41
00:03:42.804 --> 00:03:48.566
After that, the statue stopped talking.

42
00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:52.249
Swallow rested near the statue’s feet.

43
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.874
Swallow thought about telling the prince about his reed.

44
00:03:55.875 --> 00:04:01.392
She was now brown and wilted. But he stopped himself.

45
00:04:01.393 --> 00:04:10.766
"This statue doesn't need to hear another sad story!" Swallow thought.

